Region pool fragmented-memory regression
=======================================

Run regionpool after a DOS boot on a Chip-RAM-only Amiga, such as the stock
2 MiB CD32 fixture. Machines with Fast RAM return a skip result. The test
temporarily reserves its own memory to leave separated 16 KiB free ranges;
it releases every reservation before exiting.

Expected: REGION POOL TEST: 0 failures and return code 0.

The test checks observable region geometry in 32 simultaneously live
regions, growth beyond one rectangle chunk, and complete pool-memory return
after ClearRegion. Optional reservations must not invoke the counting
low-memory handler. Genuine exhaustion must still invoke normal reclamation
for the minimum allocation and report failure cleanly.

The original fixed-size pool cannot allocate even the first region rectangle
in this fixture and invokes low-memory handlers during the first phase.
